{
  "category": "Sea Slug Pokémon",
  "entries": [
    {
      "text": "It has a pliable body without any bones. If any part of its body is torn off, it grows right back.",
      "version": "diamond"
    },
    {
      "text": "It apparently had a huge shell for protection in ancient times. It lives in shallow tidal pools.",
      "version": "pearl"
    },
    {
      "text": "Long ago, its entire back was shielded with a sturdy shell. There are traces of it left in its cells.",
      "version": "platinum"
    },
    {
      "text": "When its natural enemy attacks, it oozes purple fluid and escapes.",
      "version": "heartgold"
    },
    {
      "text": "When its natural enemy attacks, it oozes purple fluid and escapes.",
      "version": "soulsilver"
    },
    {
      "text": "Long ago, its entire back was shielded with a sturdy shell. There are traces of it left in its cells.",
      "version": "black"
    },
    {
      "text": "Long ago, its entire back was shielded with a sturdy shell. There are traces of it left in its cells.",
      "version": "white"
    },
    {
      "text": "Long ago, its entire back was shielded with a sturdy shell. There are traces of it left in its cells.",
      "version": "black-2"
    },
    {
      "text": "Long ago, its entire back was shielded with a sturdy shell. There are traces of it left in its cells.",
      "version": "white-2"
    },
    {
      "text": "When its natural enemy attacks, it oozes purple fluid and escapes.",
      "version": "x"
    },
    {
      "text": "It apparently had a huge shell for protection in ancient times. It lives in shallow tidal pools.",
      "version": "y"
    },
    {
      "text": "When its natural enemy attacks, it oozes purple fluid and escapes.",
      "version": "omega-ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "It apparently had a huge shell for protection in ancient times. It lives in shallow tidal pools.",
      "version": "alpha-sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "It has strong regenerative capabilities. Even if parts of it are bitten off by fish Pokémon, it will return to normal within a few hours.",
      "version": "sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "Plankton, invisible to the naked eye, is its main food source. It comes onto the land periodically, but the reason for this is not known.",
      "version": "moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "Long ago, it had a shell on its back. There’s now a vestigial plate on its back that’s hard but thin.",
      "version": "ultra-sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "Their shape and color change, depending on their environment and diet. There are many of them at beaches where the waves are calm.",
      "version": "ultra-moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its search for food sometimes leads it onto land, where it leaves behind a sticky trail of slime as it passes through.",
      "version": "sword"
    },
    {
      "text": "The softness of its body helps disperse the force of impacts, so although its body is uncommonly squishy, it’s also surprisingly resilient.",
      "version": "shield"
    },
    {
      "text": "Eats beach sand for nourishment. Should one Gastrodon encounter another of a different color, a fierce battle will inevitably ensue.",
      "version": "legends-arceus"
    }
  ],
